LiquidCall in directcall

The speech codec is Liquid AI's Liquid-Codec (24 kHz, 12 codebooks, 12.5 frames/s,
about 1.65 kbps). The model weights and the decoder design are Liquid AI's and
are used under the LFM Open License v1.0. That license allows commercial use
only below USD 10M annual revenue (Section 5). The license text ships with the
model repository, not in this tree:

  https://huggingface.co/LiquidAI/Liquid-Codec
  https://github.com/shershah1024/liquidcodec-ane/blob/master/LICENSE-LFM-Open-v1.0.txt

The Apple Neural Engine packages are a separate conversion. The published
decoder conversion is shershah1024/liquidcodec-ane (decoder only, fixed
40-frame window). The Core ML encoder and the smaller streaming chunk are
expected from wilddolphin2025/liquidcodec-ane. scripts/liquidcall/fetch_models.sh
downloads them at setup time. This repository does not vendor the weights.

What this tree adds is the WebRTC payload, the 80 ms packet pacer, and the
macOS directcall glue. It does not re-convert the encoder or the decoder.
